  "notes": "ほどく means to untie or undo something that has been tied, knotted, or wrapped. It focuses on releasing a fastening, as opposed to ほぐす which means loosening something tangled or compressed.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: ほどける (intransitive, to come untied)\n\nASPECT (ている):\nほどいている describes the action in progress. The result \"is untied\" is expressed with the intransitive ほどけている.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {紐|ひも}をほどく: to untie a string/cord\n- {結|むす}び{目|め}をほどく: to undo a knot\n- {帯|おび}をほどく: to undo an obi sash\n- {包|つつ}みをほどく: to unwrap a package\n- リボンをほどく: to untie a ribbon\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ほぐす: to loosen, untangle (tangled/compressed things)\n- {解|と}く: to solve, to undo (broader, also used for puzzles)",
